 "observations": [
  "The page number «208» stands at the head of the page, centred, with a rule below it; at the left the number of the table, «Tab. 93», in bold sans serif, underlined. The page has no signature and no title: the folios of the manuscripts stand at the left above the double rule of the first field, in two lines of their own, «C 91v, O 147v,» and «N 58r.», the second indented, the letters raised (L01-L02).",
  "The page holds three fields, as pp. 206-207 (JP2 0238-0239): «Quinque gradus Tauri» (L03), «Decem gradus Tauri» (L15) and «Quindecim gradus Tauri» (L23), the ascendant at 5°, 10° and 15° of Taurus, with the numbers for the sextile, the quadrature and the trine, «Exagonum», «Tetragonum» and «Trigonum» (L04, L16, L24); headings and numbers in bold, the editor's «(!)» in L04 in roman. The columns begin here with the sign of the ascendant: «Taurus Scorpius Horoscopus1)», «Gemini Sagittar. Horoscopus», «Cancer Capricorn. Horoscopus», «Leo Aquarius Horoscopus», «Virgo Pisces Horoscopus» and «Libra Aries Horoscopus1)», where O has «Hore» (note 1); here each head is set from the top, one printed line to a line (L05-L07), with «Gradus aequales», printed upwards, in L05-L06, and the units in L08. The numbers are counted from the beginning of Taurus: 3° 20′ at 5° of Taurus in the first field, the oblique ascension of these 5° for the latitude 38° 30′ being 3° 20.5′ (computed with the obliquity 23° 35′).",
  "The numbers at the head of a field, as on pp. 206-207 (JP2 0238-0239), are a third, a half and two thirds of one number. In the first field 50° 54′ and 76° 21′ (L04) are a third and a half of 152° 42′, the last number of the field being 152° 43′ (L14); two thirds of it are 101° 48.7′, where the trine has «101° 70′ (!)», the 70 of all three manuscripts (note b), as if 102° 10′. In the second field the quadrature 77° 21′ and the trine 103° 8′ (L16) are a half and two thirds of 154° 42′, the last number being 154° 43′ (L22), whose third is 51° 34′, C's reading of note f; the edition's 24, from O, gives 51° 24′. In the third field 54° 36′, 81° 55′ and 109° 13′ (L24) are a third, a half and two thirds of 163° 48′ to 163° 50′, 8° 56′ more than the last number of the field, 154° 53′ (L30), whose thirds are 51° 37.7′, 77° 26.5′ and 103° 15.3′. The same three numbers stand at the head of the field of 30° of Taurus on p. 209 (JP2 0241, L24), with the quadrature 81° 45′, where the sextile and the trine are a third and two thirds of its last number, 163° 50′.",
  "The columns of Taurus and Gemini agree with the oblique ascensions from the beginning of Taurus for 38° 30′ within 10′ in the first field except at four places (below), within 20′ in the second except at 20° of Gemini (note i, L20), and within 18′ in the third; from Cancer on the columns fall below them, to 152° 43′, 154° 43′ and 154° 53′ at the end of Libra, where the oblique ascension from the beginning of Taurus is 198° 42′.",
  "Notes on the readings. Checked by the other two fields, which differ by 5° of the ascendant, and by the steps of the columns: the edition's readings are the nearer at 20° of Leo in the first field (note e, L12: the 103 of O and N against C's 104, the steps 4° 26′ and 4° 42′ against 5° 26′ and 3° 42′), in the quadrature of the second (note g, L16), at 15° of Cancer and at 10° and 20° of Libra in the second (notes k, m and n, L19, L18, L20: O's 68 against C's 67, the steps 5° 47′ and 5° 43′ against 4° 47′ and 6° 43′, the other fields having 67° 46′ and 67° 43′; the 141 and 148 of O and N against C's 41 and 147, the latter giving the steps 2° 16′ and 4° 17′ for 3° 16′ and 3° 17′), in the sextile of the third (note o, L24: O's 36 against C's 37, a third of 163° 49′ being 54° 36.3′), and at 30° of Taurus and 10°, 15° and 20° of Libra in the third (notes p, q, r and s, L30, L26, L27, L28: the 22, 141, 145 and 148 of O and N against C's 13, 41, 144 and 147; the steps of Libra 3° 13′ to 3° 15′). C's readings are the nearer in the sextile of the second field (note f, L16, above) and at 30° of Virgo in the second (note l, L22: C's 43 against O's 13, the steps 3° 45′, 3° 35′ and 3° 5′ into Libra against 3° 45′, 3° 5′ and 3° 35′; 135° 31′ in the third field); N's at 20° of Gemini in the second (note i, L20: N's 40 against O's 39 and C's 41; 40° 40′ in the other fields, the oblique ascension 40° 38′, and the steps 5° 10′ and 5° 5′ against 4° 10′ and 6° 5′ with O's and 6° 10′ and 4° 5′ with C's). At 25° of Taurus in the second field (note h, L21) O's 18, which the edition adopts, keeps the steps rising (3° 47′, 3° 56′ and 4° 2′, against 3° 47′, 3° 46′ and 4° 12′ with C's 8), while C's 18° 8′ lies nearer to the third field and to the oblique ascension (18° 12′; 18° 4′); at 5° of Gemini and 30° of Cancer in the first field (notes c and d, L09, L14) the readings differ by 1′ and 2′; none of these is decided. Note a confirms the quadrature of the first field, 76° 21′ (L04), half of 152° 42′.",
  "Without variants, in the first field: 14° 43′ and 17° 27′ at 20° and 25° of Taurus (L12-L13) lie 21′ and 35′ above, and 51′ and 45′ below, the other fields (14° 22′, 14° 8′; 18° 18′, 18° 12′), the oblique ascensions being 14° 9′ and 18° 4′, between the steps 3° 37′, 4° 23′, 2° 44′ and 4° 33′; 36° 30′ at 15° of Gemini (L11) lies 50′ and 60′ above the other fields (35° 40′, 35° 30′; the oblique ascension 35° 42′), between the steps 5° 40′ and 4° 10′; and 50° 15′ at 30° of Gemini (L14) lies 74′ and 53′ below them (51° 29′, 51° 8′; 51° 9′), between the steps 4° 22′ and 6° 30′. From Cancer on the first field lies below the other two, up to 2° 10′ at the end of Libra (152° 43′ against 154° 43′ and 154° 53′); its last number equals that of the third field of p. 207 (JP2 0239, L30).",
  "Specks above the 137 of Libra in L09, before the 53 of Cancer and after the 58 of Libra in L26, and in the left margin beside L24; not transcribed. Italics: «om.»."
